[SPEAKER_21]: Just to refresh everyone's memory about the givens of the project.

324
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:53,224
[SPEAKER_21]: So the project is under the MSBA Green School policy, which requires the minimum LEED version 4 silver.

325
00:24:56,434 --> 00:25:01,598
[SPEAKER_21]: The reimbursement, the base reimbursement requires the V4 silver minimum.

326
00:25:02,258 --> 00:25:08,823
[SPEAKER_21]: It requires that the project fully complies with the Stretch Energy Code, Massachusetts Stretch Energy Code.

327
00:25:09,543 --> 00:25:18,190
[SPEAKER_21]: It provides for a subsidy and mandates the full LEED commissioning credit criteria.

328
00:25:18,737 --> 00:25:28,028
[SPEAKER_21]: for the MEP, the mechanical systems, the building enclosure, which is what the B refers to here, and an ongoing commissioning plan.

329
00:25:29,428 --> 00:25:38,635
[SPEAKER_21]: At the same time, it requires three specific set of credits from the materials and resources and IEQ points.

330
00:25:38,695 --> 00:25:46,400
[SPEAKER_21]: Those are referred to as indoor environmental quality and healthy material points.

331
00:25:46,981 --> 00:25:48,742
[SPEAKER_21]: That's for the base reimbursement.

332
00:25:49,483 --> 00:25:53,446
[SPEAKER_21]: In order to obtain an additional 4% reimbursement,

333
00:25:55,814 --> 00:25:59,797
[SPEAKER_21]: The project needs to comply with the specialized stretch energy code.

334
00:26:00,558 --> 00:26:04,702
[SPEAKER_21]: And for that, the city would get an additional 3%.

335
00:26:05,502 --> 00:26:08,885
[SPEAKER_21]: Medford has adopted the specialized stretch energy code.

336
00:26:08,905 --> 00:26:11,407
[SPEAKER_21]: So the project will be designed to that code.

337
00:26:12,688 --> 00:26:24,018
[SPEAKER_21]: And then the second part of that 4% additional reimbursement is achieving five of the lead MR&IEQ points, which we're planning to do.

338
00:26:27,785 --> 00:26:33,148
[SPEAKER_21]: Just so everybody again, specialized stretch energy code, there's two main components of it.

339
00:26:33,408 --> 00:26:37,231
[SPEAKER_21]: One is you have to fully comply with the standard stretch energy code.

340
00:26:38,232 --> 00:26:41,494
[SPEAKER_21]: And then the second is the electrification pathway.

341
00:26:42,014 --> 00:26:50,120
[SPEAKER_21]: And as part of the schematic design lifecycle cost analysis, we are going to address that electrification pathway.

342
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:53,943
[SPEAKER_21]: The main building is looking at all electric HVAC.

343
00:26:55,276 --> 00:27:06,145
[SPEAKER_21]: And then the baseline is going to include a fossil fuel heating system and the associated costs of those two other items that are listed there.

344
00:27:06,385 --> 00:27:21,877
[SPEAKER_21]: In the specialized stretch code, if you do not do a fully all electric system, heating system, you need to have the electrification of heating readiness and you need to install the renewable energy

