974
01:24:33,526 --> 01:24:39,550
[SPEAKER_05]: And so we did not feel from a school leadership standpoint that there's a need for a dedicated space.

975
01:24:40,210 --> 01:24:42,953
[SPEAKER_05]: And CPR instruction can really happen in any classroom.

976
01:24:43,554 --> 01:24:51,504
[SPEAKER_05]: So we're able to utilize the rest of the facility for those two programs without impacting the overall ed plan.

977
01:24:53,085 --> 01:24:59,293
[SPEAKER_05]: The other modification that is being recommended is to have about a thousand square foot overall reduction.

978
01:25:00,315 --> 01:25:02,716
[SPEAKER_05]: of the locker room square footage that is allocated.

979
01:25:02,736 --> 01:25:29,121
[SPEAKER_05]: So this is something that we do see often with larger enrollment high schools, where the square footage that the MSB allows for is, in this case, a little bit overly generous in terms of being able to create a facility that addresses the facility's needs for both PE lockers as well as athletic locker space, including toilet rooms and shower rooms and all those associated spaces.

980
01:25:30,101 --> 01:25:38,683
[SPEAKER_05]: So we did look at a prototypical locker room area with the group, the leadership group that was reviewing this.

981
01:25:40,043 --> 01:25:52,046
[SPEAKER_05]: And there are some adjustments in terms of some additional doors and things that can be added to create sort of the flexible team room and locker room configurations that everyone is interested in.

982
01:25:53,047 --> 01:26:02,295
[SPEAKER_05]: But that can be done within the 6,800 square foot total, which would allow for that just over 1,000 square foot reduction to the locker room.

983
01:26:02,336 --> 01:26:07,961
