1274
01:53:00,680 --> 01:53:10,044
[SPEAKER_05]: Again, talking with district and school leadership, as well as department leadership, it was identified that digital photography

1275
01:53:10,774 --> 01:53:18,739
[SPEAKER_05]: moving forward would be the focus of the curriculum and not necessarily the chemicals that are associated with a traditional darkroom.

1276
01:53:19,399 --> 01:53:23,602
[SPEAKER_05]: I think that there are some positives there from just the health perspective.

1277
01:53:24,002 --> 01:53:31,547
[SPEAKER_05]: The things that are used to develop traditional photography are not the best things from a chemical standpoint.

1278
01:53:32,487 --> 01:53:38,491
[SPEAKER_05]: And so from a space utilization, being able to eliminate that square footage is the recommendation.

1279
01:53:41,857 --> 01:53:43,078
[SPEAKER_22]: Are there any questions, Aaron?

1280
01:53:44,878 --> 01:53:45,279
[SPEAKER_19]: Thank you.

1281
01:53:45,519 --> 01:53:48,540
[SPEAKER_19]: Just two quick questions, or two and then maybe an additional third.

1282
01:53:49,220 --> 01:53:56,964
[SPEAKER_19]: For the music storage space, is that intended to be shared between the orchestra, chorus, and the band, between those three programs?

1283
01:53:58,786 --> 01:53:59,966
[SPEAKER_05]: So yes, that's correct.

1284
01:54:00,006 --> 01:54:10,889
[SPEAKER_05]: And we have not gotten into the detailed programming, but it would include probably some type of sheet music, high density filing storage system, and then instrument storage as well for both orchestra and band.

1285
01:54:12,149 --> 01:54:25,852
[SPEAKER_19]: And then to double on that question, when it comes to the 2,000 square footage for both band and chorus orchestra, is the plan to have in square footage space for instruments and things like that in the classroom spaces already?

1286
01:54:26,731 --> 01:54:33,715
[SPEAKER_05]: Yeah, there's sort of an insatiable appetite for instrument storage within sort of the entire performing arts suite.

1287
01:54:34,556 --> 01:54:43,001
[SPEAKER_05]: So in addition to that storage room, we do oftentimes put musical instrument storage cabinets within the space themselves.

1288
01:54:44,081 --> 01:54:51,366
[SPEAKER_05]: They're actually very smartly designed because they typically can come with acoustic material at the back of them.

1289
01:54:52,106 --> 01:55:00,472
[SPEAKER_05]: So they can double up because they have open cage fronts as acoustic treatment within the space, as well as providing that additional storage capacity.

1290
01:55:01,653 --> 01:55:07,918
[SPEAKER_05]: And it can work well for anything that can get stored from violas to guitars to

1291
01:55:08,698 --> 01:55:12,120
[SPEAKER_05]: sort of range of sizes, right, of different parts and pieces.

1292
01:55:12,821 --> 01:55:13,081
[SPEAKER_05]: Awesome.

1293
01:55:13,221 --> 01:55:13,521
[SPEAKER_19]: Thank you.

1294
01:55:13,601 --> 01:55:15,983
[SPEAKER_19]: And then the final question is regarding the ensemble space.

1295
01:55:16,423 --> 01:55:18,584
[SPEAKER_19]: I know it's listed as 950 for the one space.

1296
01:55:19,465 --> 01:55:29,631
[SPEAKER_19]: Has there been any conversation or will that be a further conversation about, I know that there are many community groups that use, that are always looking for artistic community music spaces.

1297
01:55:30,392 --> 01:55:34,314
[SPEAKER_19]: And I know that obviously this is kind of centered near the community multipurpose space.

1298
01:55:35,395 --> 01:55:42,276
[SPEAKER_19]: Has that been a conversation about rentable space for the ensemble group as well as maybe even the band course orchestra space as well?

1299
01:55:43,636 --> 01:55:52,238
[SPEAKER_05]: So I don't believe that we've talked about that particular opportunity in terms of rental space, but there's no reason that we can't describe it or discuss it.

1300
01:55:53,218 --> 01:55:54,658
[SPEAKER_05]: And you're absolutely right.

1301
01:55:54,818 --> 01:55:57,159
[SPEAKER_05]: It's in the same, the right general vicinity.

1302
01:55:57,599 --> 01:56:04,520
[SPEAKER_05]: I think it'll all come down to sort of where we have access control in terms of doors and sort of credential.

1303
01:56:05,361 --> 01:56:16,493
[SPEAKER_05]: control through and making sure that there's a good separation of potential uses or accepting the fact that maybe those rentals happen outside of normal school hours as well as another opportunity.

1304
01:56:17,554 --> 01:56:21,119
[SPEAKER_05]: It's one of those scenarios where I think again we want to have some additional

1305
01:56:21,599 --> 01:56:34,843
[SPEAKER_05]: programming discussion on the performing arts side, and then also with overall building security safety first responders, just to make sure that we have sort of everyone's considerations sort of well evaluated and balanced as we go forward on something like that.

1306
01:56:34,943 --> 01:56:40,465
[SPEAKER_05]: But it is a great idea in terms of another potential revenue generating opportunity.

1307
01:56:41,106 --> 01:56:41,406
[SPEAKER_19]: Absolutely.

1308
01:56:41,426 --> 01:56:41,946
[SPEAKER_19]: Thank you very much.

