[SPEAKER_02]: We're trying to plan for as much as we can.

1450
02:09:25,900 --> 02:09:32,623
[SPEAKER_02]: But at some point, if the parking trips over some threshold, then we're going to look into needing to stack program.

1451
02:09:34,702 --> 02:09:36,723
[SPEAKER_02]: So we're close, I would say.

1452
02:09:37,604 --> 02:09:48,809
[SPEAKER_02]: And finally, we're also recommending Ken Lord can authorize removal of associated parking by program if in the event the project eliminates these programs.

1453
02:09:49,070 --> 02:09:53,332
[SPEAKER_02]: And that will let the building committee know at the next chance we get at the next scheduled meeting.

1454
02:09:54,272 --> 02:09:55,893
[SPEAKER_02]: There's a lot of information here.

1455
02:09:56,773 --> 02:10:07,198
[SPEAKER_02]: I just wanted to provide a high level and happy to answer if you have any questions, get back to you or have a discussion about what the parking might be for the project going forward.

1456
02:10:10,019 --> 02:10:10,539
[SPEAKER_04]: Thanks, Erin.

1457
02:10:11,360 --> 02:10:12,040
[SPEAKER_04]: Any questions?

1458
02:10:17,843 --> 02:10:18,143
[SPEAKER_20]: Lisa?

1459
02:10:20,870 --> 02:10:26,294
[SPEAKER_20]: Hi, I have a question about the hundred student parking spaces, how you got that number.

1460
02:10:26,374 --> 02:10:32,518
[SPEAKER_20]: I did read the PDF that was sent out earlier today, or maybe it was yesterday, but the one that we received.

1461
02:10:34,119 --> 02:10:41,443
[SPEAKER_20]: I can see that at the top of page three, there's a calculation, but it was based just on senior driving.

1462
02:10:44,590 --> 02:10:46,351
[SPEAKER_20]: It seems like the total number is fine.

1463
02:10:46,451 --> 02:10:57,958
[SPEAKER_20]: I want to preface a lot of this by just saying I hope that we are going to be advocating for good bicycle parking and that kind of scooter parking, if that seems necessary.

1464
02:11:00,299 --> 02:11:05,822
[SPEAKER_20]: But I wanted to make sure that as we're thinking about how we're laying stuff out, is 100 parking spaces for students really enough?

1465
02:11:07,888 --> 02:11:08,828
[SPEAKER_02]: It's a really good question.

1466
02:11:09,028 --> 02:11:17,651
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't think the school has a super good accounting of how students come to the site now, because we understand they're not permitted.

1467
02:11:18,431 --> 02:11:20,011
[SPEAKER_02]: Spaces are not assigned on the site.

1468
02:11:20,411 --> 02:11:27,153
[SPEAKER_02]: And so that's going to be something we talk about in a little bit of detail later on is how parking is assigned on site.

1469
02:11:29,834 --> 02:11:31,034
[SPEAKER_02]: So it's a good question.

1470
02:11:31,134 --> 02:11:32,234
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't have the answer, though.

1471
02:11:34,835 --> 02:11:34,895
[SPEAKER_02]: OK.

1472
02:11:34,915 --> 02:11:35,075
[SPEAKER_22]: Diane?

1473
02:11:36,812 --> 02:11:37,252
[SPEAKER_08]: Hi, Aaron.

1474
02:11:37,873 --> 02:11:39,734
[SPEAKER_08]: Just a quick question.

1475
02:11:39,754 --> 02:11:46,097
[SPEAKER_08]: At what point do you think we would have to tip into a stacked or tiered parking?

1476
02:11:46,117 --> 02:11:47,438
[SPEAKER_08]: And obviously, I hope we don't.

1477
02:11:47,458 --> 02:11:51,020
[SPEAKER_08]: I don't want to go anywhere near there, but I was just curious what the threshold is.

1478
02:11:52,361 --> 02:11:53,581
[SPEAKER_02]: I imagine we're approaching it.

1479
02:11:53,801 --> 02:11:59,064
[SPEAKER_02]: I don't see a scenario where we're parking more than 500 spaces on this site at grade.

1480
02:12:01,581 --> 02:12:04,603
[SPEAKER_02]: we can keep it in mind if we want to study that.

1481
02:12:06,244 --> 02:12:16,409
[SPEAKER_02]: But I think even maybe 490 spaces, I think it's going to be increasingly difficult to provide clear access around the building for first responders.

1482
02:12:16,430 --> 02:12:19,271
[SPEAKER_02]: They've been very clear that's something they wish for the site plan.

1483
02:12:20,732 --> 02:12:23,694
[SPEAKER_02]: So I think we're close.

1484
02:12:23,894 --> 02:12:28,236
[SPEAKER_08]: I just think it's important that everybody knows that, to your point, we are pushing that envelope.

1485
02:12:28,256 --> 02:12:31,038
[SPEAKER_08]: So we need to be careful, because then it's a whole new can of worms.

1486
02:12:34,305 --> 02:12:34,946
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you, Brian.

1487
02:12:35,146 --> 02:12:35,386
[SPEAKER_04]: Ken?

1488
02:12:36,607 --> 02:12:46,778
[SPEAKER_12]: I just want to say we tried to do some rough justice with the student numbers by taking the total number of spaces and kind of subtracting what we thought staff was and kind of seeing what was left.

1489
02:12:48,207 --> 02:12:53,252
[SPEAKER_12]: for a number and then what was utilized and trying to come to some justification.

1490
02:12:53,272 --> 02:13:00,178
[SPEAKER_12]: Because as Aaron said, we really didn't have any kind of way to count actually how many students were using the space because we don't permit.

1491
02:13:00,218 --> 02:13:04,722
[SPEAKER_12]: But that's kind of how we kind of sort of came to the number in the best way we possibly could.

1492
02:13:04,742 --> 02:13:07,664
[SPEAKER_22]: Thanks, Ken.

1493
02:13:07,945 --> 02:13:08,185
[SPEAKER_22]: Paul?

1494
02:13:09,897 --> 02:13:15,708
[SPEAKER_17]: Yes, what is the impact if we end up doing photovoltaic over?

1495
02:13:15,728 --> 02:13:22,760
[SPEAKER_17]: I assume that reduces the number of spots because that has some physical structure that will use up space.

1496
02:13:24,454 --> 02:13:26,836
[SPEAKER_02]: Paul, so we don't see that it will reduce the number.

1497
02:13:26,896 --> 02:13:31,259
[SPEAKER_02]: We're going to be coordinating these structures to align with the striping.

1498
02:13:31,619 --> 02:13:35,022
[SPEAKER_02]: And ideally, the structure falls on a cross.

1499
02:13:35,082 --> 02:13:38,504
[SPEAKER_02]: And so it's not eating up a large area of a parking stall.

1500
02:13:39,065 --> 02:13:39,685
[SPEAKER_02]: It's a good question.

1501
02:13:40,706 --> 02:13:45,069
[SPEAKER_02]: But I think we're able to design a structure in a way that it doesn't impact quantity of parking.

1502
02:13:45,529 --> 02:13:45,950
[SPEAKER_17]: Wonderful.

1503
02:13:46,010 --> 02:13:46,370
[SPEAKER_17]: Thank you.

1504
02:13:48,812 --> 02:13:50,593
[SPEAKER_04]: Any other questions about parking?

1505
02:13:54,225 --> 02:13:54,585
[SPEAKER_20]: Lisa.

1506
02:13:56,666 --> 02:14:01,267
[SPEAKER_20]: Sorry to ask again, because we are right there close to our limit.

1507
02:14:01,987 --> 02:14:07,629
[SPEAKER_20]: I don't see the current skate park parking area on the map.

1508
02:14:07,689 --> 02:14:15,371
[SPEAKER_20]: Is that not really considered part of the footprint of our project or is that?

1509
02:14:15,691 --> 02:14:16,831
[SPEAKER_04]: We do not own that land.

1510
02:14:17,191 --> 02:14:17,472
[SPEAKER_20]: OK.

1511
02:14:22,233 --> 02:14:22,573
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you.

1512
02:14:24,300 --> 02:14:26,641
[SPEAKER_14]: So I'm just gonna have to ask this for all the soccer parents.

1513
02:14:28,002 --> 02:14:30,723
[SPEAKER_14]: When our kids play on the back fields, where do we park?

1514
02:14:32,923 --> 02:14:37,685
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, I think that most of the parking is gonna be provided at the front of the building.

1515
02:14:38,205 --> 02:14:42,707
[SPEAKER_02]: And so we're gonna be mindful of how we plan pathways around the building up to the field.

1516
02:14:44,568 --> 02:14:47,909
[SPEAKER_02]: We imagine, we hope there's going to be some parking up there.

1517
02:14:47,929 --> 02:14:52,911
[SPEAKER_02]: We'll provide some accessible parking, but it will be a challenge.

1518
02:14:53,993 --> 02:14:54,233
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

1519
02:14:56,094 --> 02:14:59,056
[SPEAKER_04]: And maybe you'll be playing on the lower field and the parking will be right there.

1520
02:15:00,737 --> 02:15:02,618
[SPEAKER_14]: Well, hopefully they'll be playing in college by then.

1521
02:15:10,823 --> 02:15:11,103
[SPEAKER_04]: Okay.

1522
02:15:11,183 --> 02:15:12,604
[SPEAKER_04]: Any other questions about parking?

1523
02:15:16,126 --> 02:15:18,608
[SPEAKER_04]: Is there a motion to approve this recommendation?

1524
02:15:18,628 --> 02:15:22,010
[SPEAKER_10]: So moved.

1525
02:15:24,128 --> 02:15:29,169
[SPEAKER_04]: By Ken, seconded by Nicole.

1526
02:15:30,969 --> 02:15:31,650
[SPEAKER_04]: Okay.

1527
02:15:31,730 --> 02:15:32,330
[SPEAKER_04]: I'll call the roll.

