1555
02:16:06,843 --> 02:16:07,123
[SPEAKER_10]: Yes.

1556
02:16:08,405 --> 02:16:12,468
[SPEAKER_04]: 13, the affirmative, zero on the negative, two absent, motion is approved.

1557
02:16:13,249 --> 02:16:16,552
[SPEAKER_24]: Danny, before we go on, can you just clarify what the motion was for the minutes?

1558
02:16:17,575 --> 02:16:32,284
[SPEAKER_04]: The motion was to accept 477 spaces and the recommendation that Ken can formally approve removal of parking if a total program comes out of the building.

1559
02:16:33,125 --> 02:16:33,485
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you.

1560
02:16:35,006 --> 02:16:44,692
[SPEAKER_04]: And Will, if you can work with the left field team to post that parking memo in detail, the detailed parking memo on our SBC website, that would be great.

1561
02:16:45,332 --> 02:16:46,633
[SPEAKER_24]: Yep, I'll put it in the documents page.

1562
02:16:47,322 --> 02:16:48,023
[SPEAKER_04]: Great, thank you.

1563
02:16:51,266 --> 02:16:58,795
[SPEAKER_04]: Okay, Matt, do you want to take over for a quick update on our PSR comments and next steps?

1564
02:17:00,516 --> 02:17:05,259
[SPEAKER_05]: I might ask Helen to do this one, because she did it very quickly.

1565
02:17:06,560 --> 02:17:08,342
[SPEAKER_23]: A little bigger break.

1566
02:17:09,342 --> 02:17:10,924
[SPEAKER_23]: Yeah, thanks.

1567
02:17:11,164 --> 02:17:13,485
[SPEAKER_23]: And we're at the end of the meeting, everyone.

1568
02:17:14,686 --> 02:17:16,227
[SPEAKER_23]: So quick summary.

1569
02:17:16,267 --> 02:17:19,530
[SPEAKER_23]: It sounds like some of you have been able to dig into these documents.

1570
02:17:19,630 --> 02:17:20,831
[SPEAKER_23]: But similar to the PDP,

1571
02:17:21,611 --> 02:17:23,011
[SPEAKER_23]: comments from the MSBA.

1572
02:17:23,532 --> 02:17:36,816
[SPEAKER_23]: They are received as an A and a B document, the A being sort of the overarching set of comments on the entire project and report, and B is very much focused on the space summary.

1573
02:17:36,876 --> 02:17:46,739
[SPEAKER_23]: So with respect to attachment A, I did pull out some of the bigger topics, and they are noted here.

1574
02:17:46,899 --> 02:17:49,640
[SPEAKER_23]: I will not read through them, but I will

1575
02:17:50,240 --> 02:17:53,542
[SPEAKER_23]: In summary, say these are very typical comments.

1576
02:17:54,022 --> 02:17:55,022
[SPEAKER_23]: Of course you do.

1577
02:17:55,303 --> 02:18:05,427
[SPEAKER_23]: We do have the deed restriction here and again they are looking for continued updates on what that looks like and how the project team is navigating that.

1578
02:18:05,848 --> 02:18:14,812
[SPEAKER_23]: They also were looking for how the SBC determined the project delivery method as CM at risk, the cost drivers, etc.

1579
02:18:17,663 --> 02:18:31,372
[SPEAKER_23]: I think, again, we felt pretty confident in responding and being able to explain the project to the MSBA with respect to these overarching comments.

1580
02:18:32,452 --> 02:18:41,338
[SPEAKER_23]: And then with respect to the B document, and I think we did get into some of these details in the work that was done over the last few weeks and discussion tonight.

1581
02:18:42,750 --> 02:18:48,604
[SPEAKER_23]: And again, this is very much focused on the spaces, the quantity of spaces, the size of spaces.

1582
02:18:49,453 --> 02:18:51,394
[SPEAKER_23]: and how they connect to the ed plan.

1583
02:18:52,715 --> 02:19:04,861
[SPEAKER_23]: And so I do think it is a continued dialogue and it's a good way for us to understand what the MSBA is tending towards with respect to reimbursement.

1584
02:19:05,401 --> 02:19:16,627
[SPEAKER_23]: So the conversation we had around the scene shop, we don't necessarily have a solid determination at this point, but we have a clue, right, in their comments and how they,

1585
02:19:17,165 --> 02:19:24,587
[SPEAKER_23]: talked about the non chapter 74 vocational spaces and the fact that we were under in that category.

1586
02:19:24,727 --> 02:19:30,568
[SPEAKER_23]: So hopefully that's a good sign that they will reimburse for that space.

1587
02:19:31,689 --> 02:19:40,611
[SPEAKER_23]: Nothing is set in stone until the SD submission, that cost estimate, and when the project scope and budget agreement is set.

1588
02:19:40,751 --> 02:19:44,812
[SPEAKER_23]: So again, we're getting a very good indicator of where

1589
02:19:45,512 --> 02:19:48,514
[SPEAKER_23]: We all stand with respect to reimbursement on various spaces.

1590
02:19:49,074 --> 02:19:54,317
[SPEAKER_23]: And as part of the B document, an updated ed plan was submitted.

1591
02:19:55,077 --> 02:20:01,601
[SPEAKER_23]: And sounds like that is and maybe more clearly will be posted on the website for you all to look at.

1592
02:20:01,761 --> 02:20:06,023
[SPEAKER_23]: But it was included with distribution that went to yesterday.

1593
02:20:07,704 --> 02:20:13,587
[SPEAKER_23]: And excitingly enough, on the 19th, we did hear back from the MSBA that

1594
02:20:15,063 --> 02:20:27,126
[SPEAKER_23]: The project will be on the Board of Directors agenda for tomorrow morning, wherein they will vote on approving to move the project into schematic design formally.

1595
02:20:27,747 --> 02:20:29,627
[SPEAKER_23]: So that's tomorrow morning.

1596
02:20:32,568 --> 02:20:36,269
[SPEAKER_23]: Any questions on the comments, especially if you've had a chance to dig into them?

1597
02:20:37,413 --> 02:20:43,239
[SPEAKER_03]: Could I just make one comment about tomorrow's exciting meeting with the MSBA?

1598
02:20:44,400 --> 02:20:55,632
[SPEAKER_03]: Later on in the agenda for our particular project, the MSBA board of directors will be discussing an increase to their grant limits and their funding.

1599
02:20:56,893 --> 02:21:02,735
[SPEAKER_03]: which will benefit this particular project if they vote that through.

1600
02:21:02,795 --> 02:21:05,456
[SPEAKER_03]: And if it's on the agenda, it is likely getting voted through.

1601
02:21:05,516 --> 02:21:10,457
[SPEAKER_03]: So just some good news that should be coming our way after tomorrow's meeting.

1602
02:21:15,459 --> 02:21:20,040
[SPEAKER_04]: Any other questions about the MSBA feedback so far?

1603
02:21:21,801 --> 02:21:22,061
[SPEAKER_04]: Luke?

1604
02:21:23,842 --> 02:21:24,862
[SPEAKER_14]: I did want to ask that

1605
02:21:26,226 --> 02:21:42,594
[SPEAKER_14]: At some point, maybe before the next meeting, the PSR feedback is posted to the document library much in the same way as the PDP feedback and district responses were posted in an easy to find standalone link.

1606
02:21:43,415 --> 02:21:50,158
[SPEAKER_14]: And if that's not in the plan, I'll make a motion that we do that.

1607
02:21:50,618 --> 02:21:54,160
[SPEAKER_14]: But I guess first I'll check, is that part of the plan?

1608
02:21:55,314 --> 02:21:55,535
[SPEAKER_04]: Yes.

1609
